CPU capacity and Energy Model for the three Kryo clusters, from the device's
own stock runtime device tree.

The Kryo clusters are three different core types at three different maximum
frequencies (Cortex-A510 2.016 GHz, Cortex-A710 2.7456 GHz, Cortex-X2
3.1872 GHz, i.e. the EPSS LUT that qcom-cpufreq-hw reads) and no device tree
in the tree says so.  topology_parse_cpu_capacity() finds no
capacity-dmips-mhz on any CPU, raw_capacity therefore stays NULL,
topology_normalize_cpu_scale() returns before writing a scale and every CPU
keeps the default cpu_capacity of 1024.  SD_ASYM_CPUCAPACITY is then never set
(no misfit handling, no capacity-aware placement), and
cpufreq_register_em_with_opp() -> dev_pm_opp_of_register_em() fails for the
same reason a second time because it requires dynamic-power-coefficient to
build an Energy Model.  Without both, EAS is unreachable and the scheduler
treats the A510s and the X2 as equally capable.

Values are the vendor's, from the CPU nodes of the stock runtime device tree
(liuqin-audit/evidence/final-runtime.dts, the qcom,kryo nodes:
capacity-dmips-mhz 0x400/0x8cd/0x952, dynamic-power-coefficient
0x64/0x101/0x1fd).  capacity-dmips-mhz is a per-MHz rating; arch_topology
scales it by each cpufreq policy's cpuinfo.max_freq, so the values yield
cpu_capacity 278 / 833 / 1024 - the same relative performance the vendor
kernel schedules with.

Placed in the board file rather than sm8475.dtsi because the numbers are this
device's own vendor ratings, and because sm8475.dtsi here is a verbatim copy
of the sm8450-mainline file (patch 0001).  Measured before this change on the
unit (7.2.5): cpu_capacity was 1024 on all eight CPUs and
/sys/kernel/debug/energy_model was empty.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -527,6 +527,63 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * CPU capacity and energy model: the four A510s, three A710s and the X2 are
+ * three different cores at three different maximum frequencies (2.016 /
+ * 2.7456 / 3.1872 GHz, the EPSS LUT table qcom-cpufreq-hw reads), and none of
+ * the upstream device trees says so.  arch_topology's fallback is cpu_capacity
+ * 1024 everywhere, SD_ASYM_CPUCAPACITY is then never set (no misfit handling,
+ * no capacity-aware placement) and EAS stays off twice over, because
+ * cpufreq_register_em_with_opp() also wants dynamic-power-coefficient before
+ * it will build a perf domain.
+ *
+ * The numbers are the vendor's own, from the stock runtime device tree's
+ * qcom,kryo nodes (liuqin-audit/evidence/final-runtime.dts): per-MHz DMIPS
+ * ratings and capacitance coefficients.  arch_topology multiplies
+ * capacity-dmips-mhz by each policy's cpuinfo.max_freq, so these values yield
+ * cpu_capacity 278 / 833 / 1024 - the same relative performance the vendor
+ * kernel schedules with.
+ */
+&cpu0 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2386>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <509>;
+};
+
 &gpi_dma0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
